# RosterRadar

Role-aware NBA **scouting dossiers** for team decision-makers — verdict first, evidence second.

## Assignment constraints
- NBA data via chosen API; clear backend/API → frontend flow
- Opinionated, easy-to-use UI; useful to FO/scouting staff
- Small 10-day scope; GitHub repo + live deploy + write-up
- Prefer TypeScript; clean, maintainable code
- AI OK if disclosed; concept and scoring must be original

## MVP (must ship)
1. Player search
2. Dossier hero: role, fit grade, one-sentence verdict, Strong/Conditional/Poor fit, confidence
3. 4–6 role pillars as peer percentiles
4. 2 strengths + 2 risks (plain language)
5. Evidence strip (e.g. L10 vs season)
6. Collapsed methodology + loading/empty/error states

## Non-goals (v1)
Auth/teams, film, tracking, salary/cap, full roster mapper, social, live in-game tools.

## UX
- Search → Dossier only; progressive disclosure (NN/g)
- One accent; fit colors sparingly; shared percentile bars
- Calm ops + editorial hybrid (CTG seriousness + Leetify clarity structure)

## Architecture default
TypeScript + Next.js; ports/adapters (`nba/` + pure `scoring/`); Zod at boundaries; BALLDONTLIE via `NbaStatsPort`; Route Handlers return typed `Dossier` JSON; deploy (e.g. Vercel).

